1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,990
The ocean covers over 70% of the surface of our planet, though, according to the National Ocean Service, 95% of it remains unexplored.
海洋覆盖了地球表面70%以上的区域，但据美国国家海洋和大气管理局称，其中95%的海域仍未被人类探索。

2
00:00:11,990 --> 00:00:23,830
This is because under the surface is a dark and hostile environment with unrelenting high pressure, freezing temperatures and bizarre creatures in the depths.
这是因为海面之下是一个黑暗而恶劣的环境，有着持续的高压、严寒的温度，还有生活在深海里的奇异生物。

3
00:00:23,830 --> 00:00:30,810
The Census of Marine Life reports more than 17,000 species living in the deep sea.
海洋生物普查报告显示，深海中生活着超过17000个物种。

4
00:00:30,810 --> 00:00:45,360
The Greenland shark can live in depths of 7,200 feet and is a rarely seen Arctic predator said to live to 400 years old and reach 23 feet in length.
格陵兰睡鲨可以栖息在7200英尺的深海，这种罕见的北极捕食者据说能活到400岁，体长可达23英尺。

5
00:00:45,360 --> 00:00:55,230
In order to battle the icy depths, Greenland sharks have chemicals in their skin which prevent ice crystals from forming on their body.
为了抵御深海的严寒，格陵兰睡鲨的皮肤中含有特殊化学物质，能防止冰晶在身体表面形成。

6
00:00:55,230 --> 00:01:05,660
Another deep-sea creature is the giant squid, an animal that remains a mystery to scientists despite being the largest invertebrate on Earth.
另一种深海生物是大王乌贼，它是地球上体型最大的无脊椎动物，但对科学家来说，它至今仍是一个谜。

7
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:13,710
Living far below the surface, what we know has largely come from carcasses being washed ashore.
大王乌贼生活在海洋深处，我们对它的了解大多来自被冲上岸的尸体。

8
00:01:13,710 --> 00:01:21,260
Marine biologists have found that they feed on fish, squid and possibly even small whales.
海洋生物学家发现，它们以鱼类、乌贼甚至小型鲸鱼为食。

9
00:01:21,260 --> 00:01:35,660
They find prey using eyes which are ten inches wide, roughly the size of a dinner plate!
它们依靠直径达10英寸的眼睛寻找猎物，那尺寸差不多相当于一个餐盘！

10
00:01:35,660 --> 00:01:43,080
Other unusual creatures include the vampire squid, which lives 2000 to 3000 feet under the ocean and is so-called because of its dark cloak that connects its eight arms.
其他奇特的生物还包括吸血鬼乌贼，它们生活在2000到3000英尺的深海，得名于连接着八条腕足的深色“斗篷”状皮肤。

11
00:01:43,080 --> 00:01:54,470
There is also the dumbo octopus, named due to its resemblance to the elephant from the 1943 Disney film Dumbo, with its protruding ears.
还有小飞象章鱼，它的名字源于1943年迪士尼动画电影《小飞象》里的大象，因为它长着一对突出的“耳朵”。

12
00:01:54,470 --> 00:02:01,220
Another unique creature is the anglerfish known for the light that hangs from its head.
另外一种独特的生物是琵琶鱼，它因头部悬挂着一个发光器官而闻名。

13
00:02:01,220 --> 00:02:09,460
So, enjoy swimming, but don’t venture too far down – you never know what is lurking beneath!
所以，尽情享受游泳的乐趣吧，但不要冒险潜得太深——你永远不知道海底深处潜伏着什么生物！
